@startuml
title Completed-course persistence (PostgreSQL / Prisma 6)
actor Student
boundary "Course UI" as UI
control "Loopback API" as API
control "Prisma workflow" as Workflow
database PostgreSQL as DB
Student -> UI: Save courses to database
UI -> API: PUT /api/demo/courses {courseIds}
API -> API: Validate unique IDs and request
API -> Workflow: saveCourses(shared sample student)
Workflow -> DB: Begin transaction; lock student row
Workflow -> DB: Validate active courses and workflow ownership
alt Invalid selection
  Workflow -> DB: Roll back
  Workflow --> API: InvalidCoursesError
  API --> UI: 400 with recoverable error
else Valid selection
  Workflow -> DB: Remove deselected manual courses; upsert selected
  Workflow -> DB: Commit
  API -> Workflow: readCourses()
  Workflow -> DB: Read manual completed courses
  Workflow --> API: Saved IDs
  API --> UI: 200 {courseIds}
end
Student -> UI: Load courses after API restart
UI -> API: GET /api/demo/courses
API -> Workflow: readCourses()
Workflow -> DB: Query shared sample student's saved courses
Workflow --> API: Persisted IDs
API --> UI: Replace local selection
note over API,DB
Database errors return 500 and are displayed by the UI.
No authentication; local sample workflow only.
end note
@enduml
